                <section id="shader-editor-interface" class="content-section">
                    <h2>🖥️ The Shader Editor Interface</h2>

                    <p>Time to open Blender's material workshop! The Shader Editor is where all material creation happens. It's a dedicated workspace designed specifically for building and connecting shader nodes.</p>

                    <figure>
                        <div style="position: relative; display: inline-block; max-width: 100%;">
                            <img src="images/lesson_10_02_shader_editor_overview.png"
                                 alt="Blender's Shading workspace showing the four working regions: the 3D Viewport with a cube in Material Preview mode, the Shader Editor with the Principled BSDF and Material Output nodes, the Properties panel on the right, and the workspace tabs across the top."
                                 loading="lazy"
                                 style="display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0;">
                            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1920 1046" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" style="position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none;">
