                    <div class="card">
                        <h4>💡 Pro Tips for Material Library Usage</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Append vs. Link:</strong> Always use Append (makes independent copy). Link creates dependency on library file.</li>
                            <li><strong>Modify after appending:</strong> Appended materials can be freely modified without affecting library</li>
                            <li><strong>Keep library updated:</strong> When you create great new materials, add them to your library file</li>
                            <li><strong>Create category files:</strong> As library grows, consider separate files: Metals.blend, Plastics.blend, Glass.blend</li>
                            <li><strong>Share with team:</strong> Your library can be shared with collaborators—great for consistent look across projects!</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

